content.text:
Correct — `.dim-label` applies `opacity: 0.55` intentionally for secondary/helper text. It creates visual hierarchy (primary labels full brightness, secondary labels dimmer). That's expected libadwaita behavior.

If you find it too dim for your screen's contrast level, you can override the opacity in `gtk.css`:

```css
.dim-label {
  opacity: 0.75;
}
```

Tweak the value until it looks right for your display. Otherwise the theme is working as intended.

